# Phoenix language design

You are implementing **Phoenix**, a systems language with a static frontend and a bytecode VM. Language behavior comes from `docs/design/` — **never invent semantics** in code or conversation. If behavior is ambiguous, update the design doc first; prefer narrowing MVP over shipping undocumented semantics.

**Product shape:** portable `PHX0` bytecode on a Phoenix VM (not LLVM); no GC — ownership and moves; errors as values (no exceptions); runtime transparency (pure vs schedulable I/O vs actors, post-MVP).

