## MVP scope

Pipeline: **lex → parse → resolve → typeck → lower → bytecode → verify → run** on a single-process, deterministic stack VM. Every executable defines `main :: () => { … }`; compilation fails without it.

**In:** `const`/`var`/functions; numeric primitives, `bool`, tuples, `()`, raw pointers, `&T`/`&mut T` in signatures, arrays `[T; N]`, slices; `struct`/`enum`/type aliases; traits (`Name :: trait`, `Type :: impl`, `Type :: impl :: Trait`, static method resolution); `if`, `if const`/`if var`, `match`, `while`, `loop`, `break`, `continue`, `return`; arithmetic/comparison/logical operators; explicit `expr as Type`.

**Out (do not implement until MVP is accepted):** scheduler, actors, mailboxes, supervision; full borrow checker (beyond use-after-move); primitive `string` (MVP is byte-first: `u8`, arrays, slices, pointers, alloc intrinsics); std I/O, networking, rich collections; std `Option`/`Result`/`?`; JIT, hot reload, `#derive`/`@derive` codegen; deferred grammar semantics.

## Non-negotiable semantics

- Integer literals default to `s32`; `u` suffix → `u32`; float literals default to `f32`. **No implicit numeric widening/narrowing** — require `expr as Type`.
- Parameters always explicitly typed; omitted return type → `()`. `if`/`match` expression branches must unify to one type.
- Uniform `::` declarations: `Name :: struct`, `Name :: enum`, `Name :: trait`, `Type :: impl`, `name :: (…) => T`.
- **Copyable** = language marker, implicit bitwise copy (never call it Rust's `Copy` in diagnostics). **Clone** = std trait, explicit, may allocate.
- `#` = compile-time directives (`#import`, `#unsafe`, `#inline`); `@` = runtime (`@spawn`, `@send`) — post-MVP execution semantics.
- Files are modules; paths use `::`; items private by default; `pub` exports.
- **Use-after-move is a compile error**; the diagnostic must cite the move site. Full borrow checking is post-MVP.
- `Option`/`Result` are **post-MVP std enums**, not compiler builtins. MVP typeck rejects `Option`/`Result` types, `Some`/`None`/`Ok`/`Err` ctors, and `?`. Never add `Ty::Option`/`Ty::Result` to the compiler.
- Collections naming: `Array` `[T; N]` fixed-size, `DynamicArray<T>` growable — never `Vec`/`vector` in Phoenix-facing names.

## Bytecode and VM contract

- On-disk: magic `PHX0`, header, section table, payloads (`vm-linear.md`). Bytecode is portable; the VM is per-platform.
- Instructions: `opcode` + `operand_count` + operands — operands are **indices only**, never embedded strings or pointers.
- The **verifier runs before execution**: header/sections, jump targets, locals, stack depth, valid zero-arity `main` entry. A malformed module must produce a clean error, never a panic or OOB access.
